WEBVTT

00:07:58.556 --> 00:08:01.236
is a base model that we made
back in February.

00:08:01.276 --> 00:08:03.036
But watch this little video.

00:08:03.036 --> 00:08:04.236
As we begin to zoom in,

00:08:04.276 --> 00:08:07.076
you can see some of the spine
that we exposed in February.

00:08:08.156 --> 00:08:10.116
It's pretty cool, it's three-dimensional.

00:08:10.116 --> 00:08:13.436
But now watch, you can superimpose
the entire skeleton

00:08:13.436 --> 00:08:16.156
that we'd revealed in the summer.

00:08:16.156 --> 00:08:17.476
Here's the main excavation.

00:08:17.516 --> 00:08:19.236
Now we can zoom in

00:08:19.236 --> 00:08:21.916
and you can look at all
of the finer details of the bones

00:08:21.956 --> 00:08:23.756
and the three-dimensionality of them.

00:08:23.796 --> 00:08:26.196
And like magic, now we remove
the Jurassic clay.

00:08:26.516 --> 00:08:27.676
Now we zoom out

00:08:27.716 --> 00:08:31.076
and are able to see just
how complete this ichthyosaur is.